MerkleAdapterLoss
├── when investment value falls
│   ├── it keeps pending liquidity demand and caps payment by surviving NAV and cash
│   ├── it requires exact authenticated review for losses beyond configured limits
│   └── it preserves allocations and payouts occurring after the snapshot
├── when the portfolio suffers a complete loss
│   ├── it reports no assets or available liquidity
│   └── it leaves outstanding demand cancellable by the delegator
└── when a position exits before the next valuation
    ├── an unreported loss remains visible as residual stale NAV until reported
    └── unreported profit stays in adapter cash until a report makes it withdrawable
